  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 335 AM EDT Friday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Daily Chances of showers and thunderstorms \ncontinue through Sunday. In addition, heat and humidity will persist \nthrough the weekend and into early next week. \n\nWeak SW flow remains aloft for today, while at the surface high \npressure remains offshore allowing for the humidity and heat to \nincrease across the area. Temperatures this afternoon are expected \nto climb into the lower 90s across the area. Dew points are progged \nto be the low 70s inland and middle 70s along the coast. With the \nmix of heat and humidity Heat Indices will be around the upper 90s \nand lower 100s but below 105F. In terms of shower and storm chances, \na weak 700mb shortwave is expected to move across the area this \nafternoon helping to initiate storms along the Lee Trough and high \nterrain. With the weak shear these storms will struggle to move and \nonce detached from a boundary will struggle to thrive. The threat \nfor severe storms remains quite marginal for this afternoon as again \nmentioned shear remains weak. However, there will be a modest amount \nof instability with DCAPE value's approaching near 1000J/kg which \nwould give a storm the potential to produce a strong to severe wind \ngust. The greatest chance for a shower and thunderstorm will be \nnorth of I-64 and the MD Eastern Shore. Through the weekend the \nweather pattern will remain quite similar with the daily chances of \nshowers and thunderstorms along the Lee Trough and high terrain and \nSea Breeze. In addition to the showers and thunderstorms, the heat \nand humidity will persist with temps ranging in the low to middle 90s \nand Heat Indices between the upper 90s and low 100s but again \nremaining shy of the 105F Heat Advisory criteria. \n\nBy early next week ensembles hint on a more zonal pattern across the \narea with the strongest flow remaining north of the area. While at \nthe surface high pressure continues to thrive off the coast \ncontinuing to usher in heat and moisture. During the early to mid-\nweek stretch the chances of showers and storms persist with the best \nchance possibly Wednesday as a stronger cold front tries to move \ninto the area. Outside of the daily chances of showers and storms, \ntemperatures are expected to rise above normal with temperatures \npossibly reaching into the lower 90s. With dew points struggling to \nmix through the day as the high is offshore they will remain the low \nto middle 70s again allowing Heat Indices to be in the low 100s. \nWill note there is a possibility that some places could reach Heat \nAdvisory criteria Tues and Wed but confidence at this time remains \nlow.",
